  },
  "question": {
    "text": "From the top of a tower, a ball is thrown vertically upward which reaches the ground in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. A second ball thrown vertically downward from the same position with the same speed reaches the ground in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. A third ball released, from the rest from the same location, will reach the ground in _____ s."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When it is thrown upward,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>When it is thrown downward,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>36</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>When the ball is dropped,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>Alternate method,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p>"
  }
}